Z||000000||danny boy||01-20-2001||06:50 PM|||| Who has the best(worst) accident story involving a Fiero?Heres mine...<BR>    A friend of mine had an 87 coupe auto for only 24 days when this happened. He and another friend went to a bar one night.on the way home they "blew a tire" and ended up<BR>jumping a curb,hitting a small wall which launched them into the air,landing on the drivers side. They then rolled onto their top<BR>before hitting a telephone pole with the right front corner. Neither was seriously hurt. The car was totaledand the driver was arrested for DUI.The car was in near perfect condition and had ALL the origional paperwork<BR>down to the fire problem plaque.Its a shame.||||reg||9
Z||000001||kinboyatuwo||01-22-2001||12:49 PM||||Have two<BR>one a guy told me he was in<P>he rolled it on a ramp when the tire blew on the front outside<BR>so yes you can roll a fiero<P>the second looked pretty cool with little dammage<P>the driver ended up under a transport truck, dont know how?  only the roof was torn up (a lot) but the rest was fine (windshield in tact)<P>might have a pic of the second at home.  If i find it i will post it!<P>------------------<BR>"Friends don't let friends drive four doors."||||reg||11
Z||000002||fierojunky||01-22-2001||01:27 PM||||Last year i was trying to drive into work on snow covered roads (with onion skins) and got mad that everyone was only going like 20mph so trying to get into the fast lane i downshifted and the backend kicked out on me i tryed to countersteer and ended up going on the sidewalk.  only damage i did was bent two (drivers side) rims and knocked it out of alignment real bad||||reg||4
Z||000003||Raydar||01-22-2001||03:17 PM||||Back in 85-86, I happened upon an accident involving a Fiero. <BR>About a mile from my house, there was a fairly steep downhill grade. An olds Delta 88 ghetto cruiser (ya' had to be there) had stopped short to make a turn, and an 85 GT hit him from the rear and wedged itself under, like a doorstop. The butt end of the Olds was about 10 feet in the air. The rear axle was directly above the windshield of the GT. <BR>Don't think anyone was hurt badly. <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000004||Standard||01-22-2001||03:36 PM||||I wonder how often Fiero's get wedged under other cars...<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fiero_under.jpg">  <P>My worst accident was in high school with my 2m4... we had really narrow lanes in our parking lot, and I had gotten back a little late from lunch.  Headed up on of the lanes in hope of a good spot, but there weren't any so I just put it in reverse and backup up, well, kinda fast.  Looked behind me the whole way until I was getting ready to swing out.. looked forward, turned the wheel to the left and <B>crunch</B>... I know this kid stopped behind me but I'm not sure why.. Chrysler Lebaron convertible, hit it in front of the rear wheel with my pass. side rear bumber, pretty much demolished it.  hehe.  I think around $3,000 damage to his car but I don't think my insurance ever had to pay out.  Never heard anything about it after I told them what I did, and I know that kid didn't have a good driving record.  Smashed my tail light, smushed the bumper and tore up the back of the notchback panel..<p>[This message has been edited by Standard (edited 01-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||fldevel||01-22-2001||04:32 PM||||lets see .. my white 85 GT in near perfect condition .. was coming home on some really winding back roads one night and had a back tire blow while going around a sharp corner tried to stear outa hitting the guard rail and missed it by inches and ended up sling shoting to the other side of the road and parkid it between a few mail boxes and a fence and kissed the tree in the middle spun it around 3 times and ended up facing the other direction  ....(the tires on the back where firestone 225 60r 15s ) neone know if these tires where on the recall list ? <P>also that pic above just goes to show you how strong the fiero unibody can be :P||||reg||8
Z||000006||TheFiero64||01-22-2001||05:10 PM||||I've seen that newspaper clipping before, but is that a <B>no fear sticker</B> on the window? LMAO  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>88 Coupe V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||5
Z||000007||FieroJoe||01-22-2001||06:38 PM||||Wayyyyy back when the fire recall had yet to take place, my dad, a firefighter, had a first hand experience with fiero's and fires.  Only a few miles down the road from us, a (84) Fiero had started on fire in the engine, and quickly turned the magnesium decklid center plate into blinding flames.  (Mg burns as bright as arc-welding).  The guy also had some sort of Magnesium alloy rims, those too caught fire and the car was a total loss.||||reg||1
Z||000008||terryk||01-23-2001||05:55 PM||||It was on a night, just like tonight ......<p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 01-23-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||007DOUG||01-23-2001||11:55 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/87gtcrash(1).jpg"> <P>I'll bet you said something out loud when you saw this pic didn't you? Everyone does. Sends a chill down your spine doesn't it?<P>I don't always feel right about posting this pic because this crash resulted in death. <P>But... are you still going to feel invincible in your fiero tomorrow?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||HAGS||01-24-2001||10:15 AM||||Found this on a VW Passat review...<P>"An unplanned incident underscored our admiration for all that German engineering. While going 70 mph on the expressway, we encountered a Pontiac Fiero doing a 360-degree spin smack dab in front of us. Our test driver applied the brakes and quickly yanked the wheel, barely avoiding the out-of-control vehicle. (Unfortunately, another car knocked the Fiero back into us, but it only clipped off our rear fascia.) We are firmly convinced that if we had been driving almost any other vehicle, we would have hit the Fiero and serious injuries would have occurred. So three cheers to VW engineers for providing a top-notch handling performance."||||reg||1
Z||000011||Raydar||01-24-2001||11:44 AM||||Doug,<P>Do you know what that GT hit? I've only seen one other that was messed up that bad (hit a tree). I don't have the pic.<P>And no, I don't feel invincible in my Fiero. Especially since it has T-tops. Has to weaken it a bit. But even if it's just a regular Fiero, I figure I still have got to be sensible.<P>The first Fiero fatality I ever heard about was on I-75 (I think) near Atlanta. A truck tire got loose on the interstate. Don't remember if it became "unmounted", or fell off the back of a flatbed. Took a bounce and went through the Fiero's windshield. <BR>Could have happened to any car, though. <BR><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000012||Jackalrr||01-24-2001||05:30 PM||||On Friday (19th) I rolled and totaled my parents 98 blazer on the way back from skiing. I am very happy it wasn't my fiero... But one time in the fiero I did come around a corner (planning to launch up the hill to catch a civic) I downshifted to 2nd. The tires started squealing like no other.. it started sliding and turning right so I turned the wheel left to avoid going off the road, but it slid hard left and I hit a curb and bounced up into the grass. I had just gotten my rims like 2 weeks ago and I was really pissed. But there was no visable damage to the rims or car. It drives perfectly. <P>-Charlie<BR><P>------------------<BR>--------<BR>jackalrr@cinci.rr.com<P>85 GT 5spd<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fieroperformance.com/mycar21.jpg">  <BR>http://www.FieroPerformance.com||||reg||6
Z||000013||firstfiero||01-25-2001||09:47 AM||||     Back in 85 my best friend finnaly got the fiero he always wanted. He was going to the bar for pool leagues and wasn't sure where the bar was. He was sitting in the middle of a 3 lane main street at a light when he decided to pull over at a minute market to call me. He said he looked in his mirror but didn't think the firebird was going as fast as it was. It hit him dead in the side doing about 50. he was fine but his near perfect 86 se 2m6 was trashed. The insurance refused to give him all the money for it so he paid alot out of his own pocket....and now that car is mine!!! Damn glad he decided to fix it!!!!  86se||||reg||8
